WEBVTT

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/11-0
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:07.354
<v Jordan Lee>Okay, I've got us recording. Rafael, thanks. This is Alder and Finch. Congrats on the win.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/12-0
00:00:08.054 --> 00:00:09.977
<v Rafael Duarte>Thanks. This one was fun.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/13-0
00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:14.523
<v Jordan Lee>What happened at Alder and Finch that started this evaluation?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/14-0
00:00:15.223 --> 00:00:32.146
<v Rafael Duarte>They had a failed implementation. They bought an AP automation tool, I don't know which one, they never told me, and after fourteen months it still wasn't fully working. Their renewal was coming up in like ninety days and they weren't going to renew.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/15-0
00:00:32.846 --> 00:00:35.154
<v Jordan Lee>How did you hear about it?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/16-0
00:00:35.854 --> 00:00:44.315
<v Rafael Duarte>Sam Whitaker, the controller. Inbound demo request. On the first call he told me about the old vendor and the renewal date.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/17-0
00:00:45.015 --> 00:00:48.862
<v Jordan Lee>Who made the final call, and how do you know?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/18-0
00:00:49.562 --> 00:01:02.638
<v Rafael Duarte>Hannah Price, the COO. Finance reports into her. Sam told me early, "Hannah has to bless anything over fifty grand." And Hannah was the one who called me to say yes. So, pretty confident.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/19-0
00:01:03.338 --> 00:01:06.800
<v Jordan Lee>What did the customer bring up about the competitor?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/20-0
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:18.269
<v Rafael Duarte>Spendgrid was the other one. Sam was pretty open about it. After their Spendgrid demo he said, "Spendgrid's implementation plan was nine months. We're not doing that again."</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/21-0
00:01:18.969 --> 00:01:22.431
<v Jordan Lee>What changed in their questions after they'd met Spendgrid?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/22-0
00:01:23.131 --> 00:01:34.669
<v Rafael Duarte>Everything became about implementation. Who does the work, what's the plan week by week, what happens if we miss go-live. Sam wanted names of the people on our implementation team.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/23-0
00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:39.985
<v Jordan Lee>Which part of our pitch got a reaction, and which got silence?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/24-0
00:01:40.685 --> 00:01:51.838
<v Rafael Duarte>So I opened like I always do, with close five days faster. Crickets. Sam actually said, "Our close is fine, we close in six days." So that fell flat.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/25-0
00:01:52.538 --> 00:01:54.077
<v Jordan Lee>Interesting. And what landed?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/26-0
00:01:54.777 --> 00:02:05.931
<v Rafael Duarte>Two things. Hannah lit up at the store-level spend view. She wanted to see spend by store, on her phone. And then the thirty-day implementation. That's what won it.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/27-0
00:02:06.631 --> 00:02:09.323
<v Jordan Lee>What about the controls and audit piece?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/28-0
00:02:10.023 --> 00:02:12.715
<v Rafael Duarte>Fine. Neutral. Nobody objected, nobody cared much.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/29-0
00:02:13.415 --> 00:02:18.031
<v Jordan Lee>When did you first feel this was won? What happened right before?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/30-0
00:02:18.731 --> 00:02:35.269
<v Rafael Duarte>When we offered the go-live guarantee. We said if you're not live in forty-five days, your first quarter is free. My manager approved it. When I put that on the screen, Sam's whole tone changed. He said, "Okay, now you're speaking my language."</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/31-0
00:02:35.969 --> 00:02:37.469
<v Jordan Lee>Forty-five, not thirty?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/32-0
00:02:38.169 --> 00:02:45.092
<v Rafael Duarte>Yeah, we pitch thirty, but we guaranteed forty-five to give ourselves a buffer. They didn't push on it.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/33-0
00:02:45.792 --> 00:02:48.485
<v Jordan Lee>So what's the real reason we won?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/34-0
00:02:49.185 --> 00:02:58.800
<v Rafael Duarte>We took the implementation risk off the table. They got burned once, and we were the ones who put our money where our mouth was.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/35-0
00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.962
<v Jordan Lee>What did they ask for that we couldn't show?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/36-0
00:03:03.662 --> 00:03:23.662
<v Rafael Duarte>Two things. Sam wanted to talk to a customer who'd switched to us after a failed implementation somewhere else. We found one, but it took us two weeks. And Hannah wanted to see a mobile app for store managers. We only have mobile web. She was okay with it, but she asked.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/37-0
00:03:24.362 --> 00:03:28.592
<v Jordan Lee>Last one. What exact words did they use for their problem?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/38-0
00:03:29.292 --> 00:03:33.908
<v Rafael Duarte>Their pain was basically a lack of spend visibility and implementation risk.</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/39-0
00:03:34.608 --> 00:03:38.454
<v Jordan Lee>Those sound like our words. What did they actually say?</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/40-0
00:03:39.154 --> 00:03:55.308
<v Rafael Duarte>Ha, fair. Okay, Sam said, and I wrote this down, "We got burned. I'm not putting my team through another year of a half-working system." And Hannah said, "I want to know what store fourteen spent last week without emailing three people."</v>

a90a4001-8729-54c3-a446-1df9bfb201e4/41-0
00:03:56.008 --> 00:03:57.546
<v Jordan Lee>That's perfect. Thanks, Rafael.</v>
